@startuml
title Layered configuration: inputs, modules, and generated output
left to right direction
component "Reusable modules\n(options and behavior)\n\nExample:\noptions.foo.bar.path\nconfig.services.foo" as modules
component "Repository namespace\n(user-facing inputs)\n\nExample:\nconfig.ds-omega.foo.bar.path\nconfig.ds-omega.hosts.<name>" as inputs
component "Per-host / per-user glue\n(local wiring)\n\nExample:\nfoo.path = config.sops.templates.\"foo.env\".path" as glue
component "Processed program\nconfiguration\n\nExample:\nprograms.foo.settings\nprograms.foo.services" as processed
component "Generated files / runtime\n\nExample:\nfoo.conf\nuser systemd unit\ncontainer / service" as output

modules --> inputs : declare / consume contracts
glue --> inputs : supply local values
modules --> processed : evaluate
inputs --> processed : consume
processed --> output : generate / apply

note bottom of inputs
Repository namespace means the flake's own namespaced option tree,
usually config.<namespace> (for example config.ds-omega).
It is distinct from standard module namespaces such as
programs, services, and home.
end note

note bottom of modules
Concrete SOPS/OpenCode example:
docs/adr/sops-opencode.md
end note
@enduml
